    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nHint refreshes no longer retain the previous hint until the new hint is fetched which causes the hints to disappear for a short time. This is an issue for LSPs updating hints on every change such as rust-analyzer as hints will just flicker a ton when typing.\n\nai debugging tldr:\nOlder Neovim kept existing hints visible while fetching replacements. The July 5 refactor [PR#40569](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40569) started clearing them immediately, sometimes cancelling an already-running request too. That leaves a brief gap until replacements arrive and redraw.\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\n```lua\nlocal pattern = 'rust'\nlocal cmd = { 'rust-analyzer' }\nlocal root_markers = { 'Cargo.toml' }\nlocal settings = vim.empty_dict()\n\nvim.lsp.inlay_hint.enable(true)\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\n    pattern = pattern,\n    callback = function(args)\n        local match = vim.fs.find(root_markers, {\n            path = args.file,\n            upward = true,\n        })[1]\n        local root_dir = match and vim.fn.fnamemodify(match, ':p:h') or nil\n        vim.lsp.start({\n            name = 'rust-analyzer',\n            cmd = cmd,\n            root_dir = root_dir,\n            settings = settings,\n        })\n    end,\n})\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nLSP Hints should not disappear when editing the code.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1788+g09e4491a53\n\n### Language server name/version\n\nrust-analyzer 1.100.0-nightly (0ed41eb 2026-09-04) but any works\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux (rolling), Linux 7.2.7-arch1-1 x86_64\n\n### Log file\n\n_No response_",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Here is the workaround I'm using in my `after/lsp/rust_analyzer.lua`:\n\n```lua\n  handlers = {\n    ['workspace/inlayHint/refresh'] = function()\n      return vim.NIL\n    end,\n  },\n```\n\nRust analyzer seems to aggressively push these refresh requests to the client.\n\nI've been meaning to dig into how the logic works here, e.g. if its clearing the hints, then issuing a request, which might cause the flicker.",
